VALUES ('post-claim-underwriting-clause', 'Post-Claim Underwriting Clause', 'warranties', 'critical', 'Insurer reserves the right to re-evaluate the original application after a claim is filed to find errors or omissions that would justify cancelling the policy retroactively (rescission).', 'This allows insurers to take premiums for years and then avoid paying a large claim by finding a minor, unintentional mistake in the initial paperwork. It effectively makes the coverage illusory.', 'They take your money for years, but when you finally have a claim, they comb through your old application to find any tiny mistake so they can cancel your policy and not pay you.', 'Insurers should be barred from rescinding policies after a certain period (e.g., 2 years) except for documented intentional fraud.', 'We need to limit the insurer''s right to rescind this policy to cases of intentional fraud and establish a two-year limit on challenging the initial application.', 'After this policy has been in effect for two (2) years, the Insurer shall not contest the validity of the policy or rescind coverage based on statements made in the application, except in cases of documented intentional fraud.', '[0.056461472,-0.013014226,0.015798926,-0.034968853,-0.06406959,0.036877323,0.020765413,-0.006268542,0.023070067,0.004743907,0.002455209,0.00498529,0.07954992,0.004301544,0.02710297,-0.026570527,-0.015708724,-0.016687699,-0.03877962,-0.087217316,-0.014320757,0.033190884,-0.026770145,-0.056627296,0.0126098385,-0.02679029,0.030954022,-0.05389292,0.01241914,-0.014707994,0.036508888,-0.0026159317,0.0064587714,-0.009579015,-0.0020090016,0.011798048,-0.019256895,-0.012152102,-0.029887265,-0.10578164,-0.012414519,-0.005670289,-0.06065586,-0.017380405,-0.01694489,-0.011125356,-0.013272362,0.009494977,-0.04604848,0.06647634,0.008628453,0.025022078,-0.08541122,0.03614704,-0.011438813,-0.066668354,-0.023344249,-0.06721592,0.038457684,0.002538996,0.09450611,0.038079027,-0.008013366,0.03868821,0.0221