VALUES ('anti-concurrent-causation-clause', 'Anti-Concurrent Causation Clause', 'liability', 'high', 'Excludes coverage for a loss if a non-covered event (e.g., flood) occurs at the same time as a covered event (e.g., wind), even if the covered event was the primary cause of damage.', 'Common in hurricane zones. If wind rips your roof off but water also enters from below, the insurer may try to deny the entire claim because of the ''flood'' exclusion.', 'If two things happen at once—like a storm and a flood—they won''t pay for either, even if the storm did most of the damage and you''re covered for storms.', 'Coverage should apply to the portion of damage caused by the covered peril, regardless of other contributing factors.', 'We need to remove the anti-concurrent causation language to ensure that covered perils like wind damage remain protected even if other excluded events occur simultaneously.', 'Where a loss is caused by a combination of a covered peril and an excluded peril, the Insurer shall remain liable for the portion of the loss attributable to the covered peril.', '[0.043083247,0.03619375,0.014225233,0.0009988471,0.0119103575,-0.002378652,0.038819373,-0.050772574,-0.0070135854,-0.016341418,-0.009233461,-0.0075969673,-0.005730761,0.018536637,0.061887927,-0.0723584,0.02777628,0.017242799,-0.018796759,-0.03615454,0.040306974,0.008558571,-0.06629035,-0.03581834,-0.022704931,-0.023179896,0.0046000252,-0.024289146,-0.06500979,-0.04789092,0.022896232,-0.02181666,0.0115910005,-0.05269955,0.0057633044,-0.07286387,-0.03995278,-0.01755219,0.03025627,-0.03335415,-0.04291866,-0.020421717,-0.0832992,0.04259138,-0.024238618,-0.04743624,0.020806443,0.007901331,0.0004144571,0.033637494,-0.019639952,0.073900364,-0.053313464,0.020528046,0.040126912,-0.093004994,-0.011892468,-0.04245398,0.010602978,-0.011683667,0.003430473,0.054550946,-0.0013894216,0.053155493,0.020676367,-0.0029807691,-0.02274144,-0.035634782,-0.05018091,0.04008567,-0.02393095,0.027427055,-0.05683654,0.065